## P2 — Blueprint Approval Gate + Cascading Regeneration

### 2.1 Solution lifecycle state machine (`models/solution.py`)
`draft → clarifying → blueprint_ready → approved → building → built → deployed → live` (+ `changes_requested`).
- Router: after `blueprint_generator` stop at `blueprint_ready` (never auto-build).
- `POST /solutions/{id}/approve` (role ≥ `approver`), `POST /solutions/{id}/request-changes {comments}`.
- MVP build endpoint rejects unless `approved`.
- Approval snapshot: freeze artifact versions into `blueprint_versions` table (hash) so builds are reproducible.

### 2.2 Dependency graph for regeneration
```
requirements → hld → lld → er_diagram → database_schema → api_spec → code
                   └→ wireframes ──────────────────────────────────┘
                   └→ bpmn
```
- `app/services/artifact_graph.py`: `downstream(artifact_type)`; on change mark dependents `stale=True`.
- `POST /solutions/{id}/regenerate {targets, feedback, cascade: bool}` → runs only affected nodes (reuse `generation_graph` with entry-point override).
- UI: stale badges + "Regenerate affected (N credits)" button; side-by-side **diff view** between versions (JSON diff for schemas, text diff for docs, visual diff for wireframes).
- UI/UX customization: theme tokens (colors, font, radius, density) stored in `solution.ui_theme`, applied to wireframes and to the MVP template's `tailwind.config.ts`.

