## 3. Demo Script (judge-facing, ~7 min)
1. Gujarati voice note describing a clinic appointment business.
2. AI asks 4 questions (in Gujarati) + "What you missed": DPDP consent, SMS reminders, no-show fees.
3. Blueprint: HLD, ER, API, BPMN, wireframes — open "Why?" on DB choice → evidence from voice transcript.
4. Edit an assumption ("multi-branch") → impact preview → cascade regen → diff.
5. Approver role approves (show viewer can't).
6. Build → deploy (Render API + Vercel) → live URL → open on phone (Android/iOS shell).
7. Change a UI theme post-deploy → redeploy same repo → rollback.
8. Billing page: credits spent per step vs quote.

## 4. Risks / Flags
- Free LLM (`opencode/big-pickle`) may be too weak for complex enterprise builds — keep provider pluggable, measure build pass rate.
- Deploying with user PATs: scope minimally, encrypt, allow revoke.
- Existing-DB introspection must be read-only and never persist credentials.
- Don't claim full "enterprise scale" in demo without load/perf evidence.
